    "problem_statement_fixed": "Duplicating an mbuf chain whose segments come from different pools must preserve each segment\u2019s capacity and contents without overrunning a destination buffer. The behavior applies to os_mbuf_dup. The duplicate returned must be a separate chain, and for each segment in the chain it must be allocated from the same mbuf pool as the corresponding original segment, not from the pool of another segment in the chain. Each duplicated segment must have the same length and the same payload bytes as the original segment. The operation must not write beyond the payload area of any destination memblock."
